WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys, we have David Spade
on the show tonight.

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:02.602 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the funniest guys
I ever met.

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:07.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
Charlie Puth
is performing tonight.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:09.342 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:12.379
And Lily James is here, as well.
Lily James.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:15.315 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lily is the star
of the new movie

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Mamma Mia!
Here We Go Again."

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.755 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:23.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course, "Mamma Mia!
Here we go again"

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
is also President Trump's
2020 campaign slogan.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:29.829
So it's like, "Mama mia."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.865 size:78% position:39%
Actually, last night,
Trump returned home

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.400 line:92%
from his trip to Finland.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, Trump walked
into the White House

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
and immediately texted Putin
that he got home safe.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:40.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was nice.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
But after trump threw U.S.
Intelligence agencies

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:44.377 line:92%
under the bus in Finland,

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
there were protesters
outside the White House,

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.348 line:92%
shouting "Go back to Russia."

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:49.449 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:50.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
But don't worry --
the Secret Service

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:53.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
was able to get Melania
to quiet down.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.287 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.056 line:92%
"You've got things to do."

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:58.324 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's right, people
are not happy with Trump

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:03.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
for siding with Russia over
his own intelligence agencies,

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:06.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
so today, he tried
to do some damage control.

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:06.966 line:92%
But check out what happened

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
while he was
trying to tell reporters

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he still respects
U.S. intelligence.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.005 line:92%
This really happened, watch.

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Once again,
full faith and support

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
for America's
intelligence agencies.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:21.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a full faith
in our intelligence agencies.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:21.948 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.416
Whoops.
They just turned off the lights.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
That must be
the intelligence agents.

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
-What?

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:29.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dude, that's real.
That's real.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:33.493
At this point, even electricity
is distancing itself from Trump.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's --
That's when you know --

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.564 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:38.698 size:75% position:38% line:92%
The lights went out.

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, trump
is really trying to backpedal.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:43.536
He said he wants to clarify his
comments about Russian hacking,

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm not so sure
that he did that.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.172 line:92%
Take a look at what he said.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In a key sentence
in my remarks,

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:52.345 size:84% position:42%
I said the word "would"
instead of "wouldn't."

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:55.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
The sentence should have been
"I don't see any reason

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:59.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
why I wouldn't," or,
"why it wouldn't be Russia."

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:00.987 line:92%
The sentence should have been,

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:05.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don't see any reason
why it wouldn't be Russia."

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.194 line:92%
Sort of a double negative.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:13.600 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that should
clear things up.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.970 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.705 line:92%
"Would, would not, would.

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:21.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wouldn't say
it's a double negative.

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:22.609 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Wouldn't would not.

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.777 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I would not not say it."

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:25.545 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, God.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
Last night,
Putin did an interview

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:30.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Chris Wallace,
from Fox News.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:32.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a lot of people noticed
that Wallace really

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
went after Putin,
and it got pretty tense.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:35.221 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Take a look.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:38.691 size:84% position:42%
-Is the G.R.U. not part
of the Russian state?

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.260 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-[ Speaking Russian ]

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.361 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'll get to it.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just have a little --
a little bit of patience,

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:44.697 line:92%
and you'll get a full answer.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:47.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm not asking
whether they influenced.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.001 line:92%
I am asking whether they tried.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:51.237
-If you'll have some patience,
you'll hear the entire response.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Whoa.
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
Good for him.
He wasn't afraid to stand up

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.176
to Putin,
despite knowing his reputation.

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:59.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
Anyways, let's check in
on Chris Wallace's show today.

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:01.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back to
"Special Report"

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:04.250 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
with Chris Wallace.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.220 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.488 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, I'm sure...

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sure he's fine,
I'm sure he's fine.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's great.
[ Applause ]

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:15.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
Get this, guys --
a brewery in Finland

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:16.596 line:92%
actually created a special beer

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:19.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
in honor of yesterday's
Trump/Putin summit.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:20.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
When they heard that,
some other beers

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.936 size:78% position:39%
wanted to commemorate
the summit, as well,

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:24.103 line:92%
so they released new slogans

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
that were inspired
by the meeting.

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:29.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
Check these out.
Guinness' new slogan is...

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
There you go.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.113 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Next up.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.916 line:92%
Miller Lite's new slogan is...

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:40.420 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.289 line:92%
Next, O'Doul's new slogan is...

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:48.328 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:51.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
And finally, Samuel Adams's
new slogan is...

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:55.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
There you go.
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:58.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
Interesting.
That's...

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hear that,
in honor of World Emoji Day,

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:02.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
Apple is actually releasing
a bunch of new emojis,

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:05.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
like a peacock,
a mango, and a cupcake.

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:07.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, here with his own ideas
for new emojis

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
is our World Emoji Day
correspondent,

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:11.517 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Julio Torres, everybody.

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:14.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪♪♪

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wow.
-Wow.

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:19.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Julio Torres is here.
Welcome back.

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:20.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hello.
-Welcome back.

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:23.830
Julio, you have been here a few
times with some great ideas,

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:27.333
and I hear that now you have
some suggestions for new emojis.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I do.
-Okay, good.

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:29.969 line:92%
We would love to hear them.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, well, you know how
there's an emoji

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:34.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's like a little face with
its tongue sticking out?

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:36.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-Well how about one

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:37.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
that has
it's tongue sticking out

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.946
but the tongue has a piercing,
and he's asking his boyfriend,

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:42.448
"Wait.
Does this look infected to you?"

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.717 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:47.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Interesting.
Now...

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:48.021 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:49.989
There are other examples, right?
Of new emojis?

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:53.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yes, yes, of course.
They get simpler.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:53.526 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Um, okay.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
How about an emoji
we can all use?

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, for example, a Hobbit
holding that ring

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:00.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
from "Lord of the Rings"
and being like,

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:04.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, I actually
don't do gold, but thank you."

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.171 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:07.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm shocked that
that doesn't exist already.

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:08.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Do you have any other

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:11.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
maybe simpler,
more simpler emoji ideas?

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:12.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I do.
How about one of

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:15.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
the planet Jupiter
learning that scientists

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:21.020
refer to it is a gassy giant
and being like, "Wow, okay."

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.924 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:28.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or, or, or -- okay.
Well, how about one

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:29.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's a copy of
"The New York Times"

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:32.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a square-shaped hole
where a bad review used to be,

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:35.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
which your assistant cut out
to protect your feelings.

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:36.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-These are all great emojis.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:39.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm shocked that
they don't exist already.

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:41.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Or, or, or perhaps
one of someone

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:44.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
who sprained their wrists
by furiously writing a check,

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
tearing it from the checkbook
and going,

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.680 line:92%
"I trust this will suffice."

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.082 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:51.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"I trust this will suffice."
Yeah.

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:53.886
These are great, Julio, but
we only have time for one more.

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:56.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am getting a note
from our director.

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:56.989 line:92%
We only have time for one more.

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:59.258
-I don't think I heard it,
but, okay, just one more.

00:05:59.258 --> 00:05:59.792 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:03.429
How about an emoji
of a Disney princess being like,

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:06.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Wait. What? I have to pose
for another backpack?

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:08.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
When does
this contract even end?"

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:09.102 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:09.102 --> 00:06:12.805
-"Tonight Show" World Emoji Day
correspondent Julio Torres!

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:13.539 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:16.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
My hand's good.
Everything's great.

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:17.243 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Julio Torres.

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:20.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
Julio Torres,
everybody, right there.

00:06:20.513 --> 00:06:22.882
And finally, everybody,
I read about a couple in Florida

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:25.618
that's getting married,
and instead of wedding presents,

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:28.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
they've asked
for money to buy goats.

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:29.222 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.990 size:88% position:44%
Even crazier, one couple
they invited was like,

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Finally, a chance
to regift this goat."

00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:34.260 line:92%
We have a great show tonight.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
Give it up for
The Roots, everybody!

